'''Princess Kiko''' ({{nihongo|Kiko-naishinnō|紀子内親王}}; born 12 April 2006) is the second child and only daughter of Emperor [[Emperor Masahito|Masahito]] and Empress Michiko. She occupies the third position in the line of succession to the Wisteria Throne. Within the Imperial family's modern framework of "Functional Royalty," Kiko has distinguished herself through her commitment to environmental engineering and urban ecology. Her work focuses on reconciling Okaiken’s heavy industrial output with sustainable land management, a field she describes as "The Living Forge."

==Early life and education==
Princess Kiko was born in the Imperial Palace in Okami during the height of the "Silent Years" of her father’s reign. Unlike the more public upbringing of her elder brother Tomohito, Kiko’s early years were marked by a private education that emphasized the Sanese tradition of ''Satoyama''—the balanced relationship between human habitations and the natural world. 

She attended the Gakushūin Girls' Senior High School, where she led the "Grey to Green" initiative, a student-led project aimed at introducing vertical gardens into the school's concrete-heavy architecture. In 2024, she followed her brother’s precedent by enrolling in the [[Okami Imperial University]], specifically within the Faculty of Environmental Design. She is currently pursuing a Bachelor of Landscape Architecture (B.L.A.), focusing on the remediation of industrial brownfields. Her academic work often explores how abandoned steel foundries can be converted into "Carbon Sinks" for the capital city.

==Ecological initiatives==
Kiko’s public duties are almost exclusively centered on the intersection of ecology and urban planning. In late 2024, she was appointed as the honorary patron of the Okaiken Green Building Council. In this role, she has advocated for the mandatory inclusion of native flora in new industrial zones, arguing that a "Steel State" requires "Green Lungs" to maintain national health.

Her most significant contribution to date is the "Komorebi Protocol," a series of recommendations she co-authored for the Ministry of Land and Infrastructure. The protocol suggests utilizing traditional Sanese irrigation techniques to manage modern urban runoff in Okami. Unlike the ceremonial roles of past princesses, Kiko frequently participates in on-site field surveys, often seen in the domestic press wearing high-visibility gear and carrying architectural blueprints.

==Architectural preservation==
[[File:Princess Kiko.png|thumb|left|200px|Princess Kiko Posing for the Official Imperial Family album.]]
Beyond her ecological work, the Princess is a vocal advocate for the preservation of Meiji-era industrial architecture. She views these structures not as relics of the past, but as essential components of Okaiken’s "Forge" identity. She has funded several projects aimed at retrofitting historical brick warehouses with modern solar-glass technology, ensuring that the nation's aesthetic history survives within a sustainable future.

==Public image==
Princess Kiko is often characterized as the "Soft Conscience" of the Imperial House. While her father and brother Tomohito project an image of unyielding strength, Kiko provides a visual and intellectual counterpoint that emphasizes growth, adaptation, and harmony. She is widely popular among the younger generation of Sanese citizens, who view her academic rigor and environmental focus as a modern interpretation of the traditional imperial role of "Guardian of the Land."

